{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can install React Query via "},{"type":"link","href":"https://npmjs.com/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\nor a good ol' "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" via\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://esm.sh/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESM.sh"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"npm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add @tanstack/react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"bun add @tanstack/react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"deno add @tanstack/react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is compatible with React v18+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/simple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"simple"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" examples!"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cdn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're not using a module bundler or package manager, you can also use this library via an ESM-compatible CDN such as "},{"type":"link","href":"https://esm.sh/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESM.sh"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Simply add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"type":"text","value":" tag to the bottom of your HTML file:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script type=\"module\">\n  import React from 'https://esm.sh/react@18.2.0'\n  import ReactDOM from 'https://esm.sh/react-dom@18.2.0'\n  import { QueryClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@tanstack/react-query'\n</script>","lang":"html"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can find instructions on how to use React without JSX "},{"type":"link","href":"https://react.dev/reference/react/createElement#creating-an-element-without-jsx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"here"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"requirements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Chrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":" yourselves."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recommendations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is recommended to also use our "},{"type":"link","href":"../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESLint Plugin Query"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"bun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query","lang":"bash"}],"headings":[{"id":"npm","text":"NPM","level":3},{"id":"cdn","text":"CDN","level":3},{"id":"requirements","text":"Requirements","level":3},{"id":"recommendations","text":"Recommendations","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou can install React Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com/),\nor a good ol' `<script>` via\n[ESM.sh](https://esm.sh/).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\ndeno add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Compatibility'\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v18+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](./examples/simple) or [basic](./examples/basic) examples!\n\n[//]: # 'Compatibility'\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager, you can also use this library via an ESM-compatible CDN such as [ESM.sh](https://esm.sh/). Simply add a `<script type=\"module\">` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n[//]: # 'CDNExample'\n\n```html\n<script type=\"module\">\n  import React from 'https://esm.sh/react@18.2.0'\n  import ReactDOM from 'https://esm.sh/react-dom@18.2.0'\n  import { QueryClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@tanstack/react-query'\n</script>\n```\n\n> You can find instructions on how to use React without JSX [here](https://react.dev/reference/react/createElement#creating-an-element-without-jsx).\n\n[//]: # 'CDNExample'\n\n### Requirements\n\nReact Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config\n\n```\nChrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77\n```\n\n> Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from `node_modules` yourselves.\n\n### Recommendations\n\nIt is recommended to also use our [ESLint Plugin Query](../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query.md) to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: installation\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nYou can install React Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com/),\nor a good ol' `<script>` via\n[ESM.sh](https://esm.sh/).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\ndeno add @tanstack/react-query\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Compatibility'\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v18+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](./examples/simple) or [basic](./examples/basic) examples!\n\n[//]: # 'Compatibility'\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager, you can also use this library via an ESM-compatible CDN such as [ESM.sh](https://esm.sh/). Simply add a `<script type=\"module\">` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n[//]: # 'CDNExample'\n\n```html\n<script type=\"module\">\n  import React from 'https://esm.sh/react@18.2.0'\n  import ReactDOM from 'https://esm.sh/react-dom@18.2.0'\n  import { QueryClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@tanstack/react-query'\n</script>\n```\n\n> You can find instructions on how to use React without JSX [here](https://react.dev/reference/react/createElement#creating-an-element-without-jsx).\n\n[//]: # 'CDNExample'\n\n### Requirements\n\nReact Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config\n\n```\nChrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77\n```\n\n> Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from `node_modules` yourselves.\n\n### Recommendations\n\nIt is recommended to also use our [ESLint Plugin Query](../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query.md) to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query\n```\n"}
